--------------------

Model of substitution: GTR+F+G4

Rate parameter R:

  A-C: 2.1226
  A-G: 11.7032
  A-T: 2.7535
  C-G: 2.8374
  C-T: 19.7592
  G-T: 1.0000

State frequencies: (empirical counts from alignment)

  pi(A) = 0.3446
  pi(C) = 0.1304
  pi(G) = 0.09982
  pi(T) = 0.4251

Rate matrix Q:

  A   -0.6298   0.06667    0.2813    0.2819
  C    0.1761    -2.267    0.0682     2.023
  G    0.9711   0.08912    -1.163    0.1024
  T    0.2285    0.6206   0.02404   -0.8731

Model of rate heterogeneity: Gamma with 4 categories
Gamma shape alpha: 0.3402

 Category  Relative_rate  Proportion
  1         0.009112       0.25
  2         0.1359         0.25
  3         0.6575         0.25
  4         3.197          0.25
Relative rates are computed as MEAN of the portion of the Gamma distribution falling in the category.

